VegaChart for A2UI v0.9

index.ts and vegaChart.ts are copied from the A2UI repository
(https://github.com/a2ui-project/a2ui, commit 825beac: typescript/catalogs/vegachart/
src/components/vegaChart.ts and src/v0_9/index.ts), Copyright 2024 Google LLC, licensed
under the Apache License 2.0 (see LICENSE).

Changes by the explorer project:
- vegaChart.ts imports A2uiLitElement from '@a2ui/lit/v0_9' instead of
  '@a2ui/web_core/v1_0', which does not export it in @a2ui/*@0.14.0.
- The v1.0 type import (VegaChartV1Api) is removed; the element is typed for v0.9 only.
- Relative imports are adjusted for the flat directory.
- Clickable marks (explorer SPEC §15): an optional `action` prop ({source, rows, drillable}); a click
  on a mark whose datum has a clickable `_row` dispatches `drill` or `ask` through the component
  context, and such charts get a pointer cursor (a line chart's points, not its line) and a hint
  line saying what a click does. A click on a line mark itself is ignored.
- Theme (explorer SPEC §16): the default config is built from the page's CSS custom properties
  (`themedChartConfig`, passed to `transformSpec` as `baseConfig`), and the chart renders again
  when `prefers-color-scheme` changes.
- Boards and new Visuals (explorer SPEC §18): the Ask confirmation label comes from the datum's
  `_label` when present; a full Vega spec (`isFullVega`) gets a numeric width
  (`FULL_VEGA_FALLBACK_WIDTH`) when the container is unmeasured, since only Vega-Lite accepts
  'container'; and the themed config gives text marks the card colour (`text.fill` from `--panel`).
- Polish (explorer SPEC §22): the themed config also sets rounded bar ends, no axis domain or tick
  lines, dashed y gridlines only, mono axis and legend labels, and card-coloured rect strokes. Before
  rendering, `withArea` layers a gradient area under a single-series line and `withHover` gives bar
  unit specs a hover fade (both skip specs they can't safely change), clicks on `area` items are
  ignored like `line` items, and the embed passes `tooltip: {theme: 'explorer'}`.
  `withTileStroke` gives full-Vega rect marks without a stroke a card-coloured one (Vega ignores the
  config's `rect.stroke` when a mark encodes `fill`).
